  "keyTitle": "Operating System and Workstation Environment",
  "keyShortInfo": "Assess how operating systems and workstations are provisioned, maintained, and protected, including remote use, shared storage, device encryption, and operational logging.",
  "keyDescription": "This set covers the working environment used by staff and administrators, including local, diskless, and remote workstations. It considers asset identification, approved system images, patching, local data, shared file systems, and the handling of device decryption keys. Its questions should identify the devices and review period in scope and connect each condition to configuration or operational evidence. Privileged access is addressed in SFS 1, recovery testing in SFS 2, and central monitoring in SFS 6.",
  "keyWords": "operating systems, workstations, endpoint inventory, provisioning, patching, diskless clients, remote desktops, shared storage, device encryption, endpoint logging",
  "promptAi": "Help an author develop sixteen clear yes/no scoring factors for Operating System and Workstation Environment. Use this set's description and boundaries. For each proposed factor, state one condition, the system scope, evidence period, required evidence, pass/fail criterion, and acceptable alternatives. Keep questions within 512 characters, flag missing evidence for review, and do not invent assessment results or claim compliance.",
